From: VDR-Suite S1 native SearchTimer identity
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] epgsearch: persist native rule generations and expose locked observation
Upstream-base: 0118b4129c3601c04c7483f2fd04b604d4a2a980
Depends-on: 0001-searchtimer-owner-lock-legacy-writers.patch

The existing epgsearch.conf colon-delimited rule format stays unchanged.
Persist an immutable random sg_<32 lowercase hex> generation in a comment
before each native search rule. Old plugins ignore the comments. On upgrade
after an old plugin resaved the file, a new generation is minted rather than
reusing an old ID. Missing/duplicate/invalid metadata is never attested as
durable. Native generation is not inherited from templates or rule copies.

The read-only Epgsearch-searchtimer-observe-v1.0 cPlugin::Service returns
the native generation and rule snapshot under the epgsearch list lock.
This is NOT native CAS; there is no revision or conditional write yet.
DO NOT enable Public-v1 UPDATE/ACTIVATE/DEACTIVATE/DELETE from this patch.

Requires native plugin compile/tests and an explicit packaging gate.
No live yaVDR changes, no upstream changes, and no change to main.

